# Internal working area: raw agent reports, scratch research, experiments, private media
.orimera/
# Slashless on purpose. In the sibling worktree orimera-person-consent, .exulanica is a symlink
# into this checkout's blob store, so git records it as a blob and a directory-only rule misses
# it (MEASURED 2026-09-07: git status there reported '?? .exulanica', and committing it would
# have stored a machine-specific absolute path). Slashless still matches the real directory
# here, so one rule covers both the directory and the symlink.
.exulanica

# Secrets and environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.key.example
secrets/
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Raw personal media and sensitive derivatives
media/raw/
media/private/
**/raw_media/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.wav
*.m4a
*.aac
!docs/assets/**/*.mp4

# Sensitive derived artifacts
transcripts/
**/transcripts/
embeddings/
**/*.embeddings
**/*.npy
**/face_*.bin
**/voice_*.bin

# Model caches and weights
models/
# ...but exulanica/models is source code, not a weight cache. Without this negation the whole
# model package is invisible to git and, because hatchling honours these rules, absent from the
# built wheel. `uv run exulanica-preflight` on an installed copy is what noticed.
!exulanica/models/
checkpoints/
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
.cache/
~/.cache/

# Reconstruction outputs
reconstructions/
sparse/
dense/
*.ply
*.splat
*.ksplat
*.spz
colmap_output/

# Raw API responses containing user data
**/api_responses/
*.raw.json

# Local database and object store state
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
pgdata/
minio_data/
.localstack/

# Temporary GPU job artifacts
job_artifacts/
tmp/
.tmp/

# Standard build/tooling
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
.turbo/
coverage/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local agent tooling config, not part of the project
.claude/
.cursor/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Two different things are held out of this repository under docs/, and only one of them is
# named here.
#
# THE FIRST IS OPERATOR PROCESS, and the rules below name it: briefs, records, patches and a
# handful of documents at the docs/ root. Every one is matched by a rule in THIS file, which is
# tracked, so a clone can see what is missing and why, and a test in
# tests/test_documentation_links.py reads that back from git rather than trusting this sentence.
#
# THE SECOND IS A SET OF EVALUATION CAMPAIGNS under docs/evaluation/ that were run locally and
# not published: the record and the artifacts it binds exist only on the machine that ran them.
# THOSE ARE EXCLUDED PER CLONE IN .git/info/exclude AND DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED HERE, so this
# repository does not carry their names. The consequence is worth stating rather than leaving to
# be discovered: no clone can enumerate them, and a rule that lives in one checkout cannot stop a
# different checkout committing them by accident. What a reader can see is the subset this
# repository itself points at, named one by one in tests/test_documentation_links.py, because a
# pointer nobody can follow is the only part of this that costs a reader anything.
#
# Operator process. Kept on disk for evidence tests. Not published.
docs/briefs/
docs/records/
# The four named patches below ARE published, and the rule spells the directory's contents rather
# than the directory because git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a `docs/patches/`
# rule cannot be undone by a negation inside it. Each of the four is a plain diff against
# web/packages/app/src/main.ts with no operator process in it, and one is named inside an immutable
# evaluation record, which pins its path permanently: while it is absent that record is stranded
# and cannot be repaired, because repairing it would change a digest other records bind.
docs/patches/*
!docs/patches/companion-memory-main.patch
!docs/patches/companion-proposals-main.patch
!docs/patches/companion-question-main.patch
!docs/patches/manual-person-review-main.patch
docs/first-place-2026-09-11.md
docs/judge-access.md
docs/naming.md
docs/infrastructure-backlog.md
docs/engineering-log.md
docs/engineering-log-reconstructed.md
docs/goal-brief-2026-09-05-unblocked-backend-program.md
docs/goal-brief-2026-09-08-remaining-work.md
docs/phase-10-tickets.md
docs/reference-gpu-compute.md
docs/frontier-demonstration.md
docs/reconstruction-throughput.md
